# ZAIM Tor config.
#
# Two jobs, deliberately separate:
#   1. A v3 onion service so someone can reach ZAIM without their request
#      crossing the clearnet, without DNS, and without us or their network
#      learning their address.
#   2. A SOCKS port on the compose network, so the API can optionally send
#      lightwalletd traffic through Tor. Off by default on the API side.

# Reachable only on the compose network. This port is never published to the
# host, so nothing outside the docker network can use it as an open proxy.
SocksPort 0.0.0.0:9050
SocksPolicy accept 172.16.0.0/12
SocksPolicy accept 192.168.0.0/16
SocksPolicy reject *

# Persisted on a named volume, so the .onion address survives a rebuild.
HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/zaim
HiddenServiceVersion 3
HiddenServicePort 80 zaim-web:80

# We are a client and a service, never a relay.
ClientOnly 1
Log notice stdout
